  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "In Bohr&#39;s atomic model, the electron is assumed to revolve in a circular orbit of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the speed of electron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the current associated with the electron will be__________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi><mo>.</mo></math> [Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math> as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "112",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Time taken to revolve in circular orbit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Now, current associated with the electron is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math><br />Hence, the current is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>112</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math>.</p>",
